IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Circuit Layouts Act 1989 (Cth) — THE NOUNS, THE RULES AND THE TOP-LEVEL
-- GOAL. Source: ../registers/source-bundle/C2004A03776.txt (compilation prepared on 12
-- October 2012). The person who copies, makes or deals in chips asks: "Is this
-- layout protected, and until when; does what I do infringe; can damages be
-- awarded against me; until when can I be sued?"

§ `Nouns`

-- s 17(a)-(c), s 19(1)-(3): the act I do.
DECLARE `My act` IS ONE OF
    `copying the layout in a material form`
    `making an integrated circuit in accordance with the layout`
    `commercially exploiting the layout, a copy or a circuit in Australia`

-- ss 21-23: the purpose of a copy or circuit I make.
DECLARE `My purpose` IS ONE OF
    `trade or another purpose`
    `my private use`
    `research or teaching`
    `evaluating or analysing the layout`

DECLARE `Layout case` HAS
    -- s 5 eligible layout, s 11 originality
    `the day the layout was made`                                   IS A DATE
    `the year it was first commercially exploited`                  IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `its making involved a creative contribution by the maker`      IS A BOOLEAN
    `it was commonplace when made`                                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the maker was an eligible person when it was made`             IS A BOOLEAN
    `it was first commercially exploited in Australia or an eligible foreign country` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 19
    `my act`                                                        IS A `My act`
    `the day I do it`                                               IS A DATE
    `I have the owner's licence`                                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `I know or ought reasonably to know I am not licensed`          IS A BOOLEAN
    -- ss 21-23
    `my purpose`                                                    IS A `My purpose`
    `my private copies are exploited or distributed to the owner's prejudice` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 20
    `I acquired the circuit not knowing, and not reasonably expected to know, it was unauthorised` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I have since become aware, or could reasonably be expected to be` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I pay the owner equitable remuneration`                        IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 24
    `I acquired it through the owner's own or licensed commercial exploitation` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 25
    `I act for the Commonwealth for defence or security, after it failed to get a licence on reasonable terms` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 27(3)
    `I was not aware, and had no reasonable grounds to suspect, that it infringed` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 7: the Proclamation date of Part II (not in the deposited text)
    `the commencement of Part II`                                   IS A DATE

DECLARE `Layout position` HAS
    `the layout is protected`                                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `the protection period ends on`                                 IS A DATE
    `my act infringes`                                              IS A BOOLEAN
    `an action lies against me`                                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `damages may be awarded against me`                             IS A BOOLEAN
    `the last day I can be sued`                                    IS A MAYBE DATE

§ `Rules`

-- s 11: not original if no creative contribution, or commonplace.
@ref s 11
GIVEN c IS A `Layout case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the layout is original` c IF
        c's `its making involved a creative contribution by the maker`
    AND NOT (c's `it was commonplace when made`)

-- s 5 eligible layout: an original layout whose maker was an eligible person
-- when it was made (s 6, s 15), or first commercially exploited in Australia or
-- an eligible foreign country.
@ref s 5 eligible layout
GIVEN c IS A `Layout case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the layout is eligible` c IF
        `the layout is original` c
    AND (   c's `the maker was an eligible person when it was made`
         OR c's `it was first commercially exploited in Australia or an eligible foreign country`)

-- s 5 protection period: from the day made (s 10(b)) to the end of the tenth
-- calendar year after the year of first commercial exploitation, if that was
-- within 10 calendar years after the year made; otherwise to the end of 10
-- calendar years after the year made.
@ref s 5 protection period
GIVEN c IS A `Layout case`
GIVETH A DATE
`the end of the protection period for` c MEANS
    CONSIDER c's `the year it was first commercially exploited`
    WHEN JUST y THEN
        IF y AT MOST (DATE_YEAR (c's `the day the layout was made`) PLUS 10)
        THEN Date 31 12 (y PLUS 10)
        ELSE `the default end for` c
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `the default end for` c

GIVEN c IS A `Layout case`
GIVETH A DATE
`the default end for` c MEANS
    Date 31 12 (DATE_YEAR (c's `the day the layout was made`) PLUS 10)

@ref s 17
GIVEN c IS A `Layout case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `my act is within the protection period` c IF
        `the layout is eligible` c
    AND c's `the day I do it` AT LEAST c's `the day the layout was made`
    AND c's `the day I do it` AT MOST `the end of the protection period for` c

-- s 19(1)-(3): without the owner's licence; for commercial exploitation, only
-- if I know or ought reasonably to know I am not licensed.
@ref s 19
GIVEN c IS A `Layout case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 19 is met` c IF
        `my act is within the protection period` c
    AND NOT (c's `I have the owner's licence`)
    AND (   NOT (c's `my act` EQUALS `commercially exploiting the layout, a copy or a circuit in Australia`)
         OR c's `I know or ought reasonably to know I am not licensed`)

-- s 20: innocent commercial exploitation of an unauthorised circuit, until I
-- become aware, unless I then pay equitable remuneration.
@ref s 20
GIVEN c IS A `Layout case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 20 protects me` c IF
        c's `my act` EQUALS `commercially exploiting the layout, a copy or a circuit in Australia`
    AND c's `I acquired the circuit not knowing, and not reasonably expected to know, it was unauthorised`
    AND ((NOT (c's `I have since become aware, or could reasonably be expected to be`)) OR c's `I pay the owner equitable remuneration`)

-- ss 21-23: copies and circuits made for private use (unless exploited or
-- distributed to the owner's prejudice), for research or teaching, or for
-- evaluating or analysing the layout.
@ref ss 21-23
GIVEN c IS A `Layout case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `my purpose excuses the making` c IF
        NOT (c's `my act` EQUALS `commercially exploiting the layout, a copy or a circuit in Australia`)
    AND (   (c's `my purpose` EQUALS `my private use` AND NOT (c's `my private copies are exploited or distributed to the owner's prejudice`))
         OR c's `my purpose` EQUALS `research or teaching`
         OR c's `my purpose` EQUALS `evaluating or analysing the layout`)

-- s 24: exhaustion by the owner's own or licensed commercial exploitation.
@ref s 24(1)
GIVEN c IS A `Layout case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 24 protects me` c IF
        c's `my act` EQUALS `commercially exploiting the layout, a copy or a circuit in Australia`
    AND c's `I acquired it through the owner's own or licensed commercial exploitation`

@ref ss 19-25
GIVEN c IS A `Layout case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `my act infringes` c IF
        `section 19 is met` c
    AND NOT (`section 20 protects me` c)
    AND NOT (`my purpose excuses the making` c)
    AND NOT (`section 24 protects me` c)
    AND NOT (c's `I act for the Commonwealth for defence or security, after it failed to get a licence on reasonable terms`)

-- s 7: no action under Part III for an act before Part II commenced.
@ref s 7
GIVEN c IS A `Layout case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an action lies` c IF
        `my act infringes` c
    AND c's `the day I do it` AT LEAST c's `the commencement of Part II`

-- s 27(3): an innocent infringer is liable to an account of profits, not damages.
@ref s 27(2)-(3)
GIVEN c IS A `Layout case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `damages may be awarded` c IF
        `an action lies` c
    AND NOT (c's `I was not aware, and had no reasonable grounds to suspect, that it infringed`)

-- s 28: not "after the end of 6 years after the day when the infringement took
-- place": the last day is the corresponding day 6 years later (28 February for
-- 29 February).
@ref s 28
GIVEN c IS A `Layout case`
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the last day to sue for` c MEANS
    IF `an action lies` c
    THEN JUST (`add months` (c's `the day I do it`) 72)
    ELSE NOTHING

@ref ss 5, 7, 11, 17, 19-25, 27-28
@export default The position of a person who copies a circuit layout, makes a chip to it, or commercially exploits it in Australia, under the Circuit Layouts Act 1989 (Cth): whether the layout is protected (an original layout of an eligible maker, or first exploited in Australia or an eligible country) and when its protection period ends (the end of the 10th calendar year after first exploitation within 10 years of making, otherwise 10 calendar years after making); whether my act infringes (s 19), unless I am licensed, an innocent acquirer (s 20), making for private use, research, teaching or evaluation (ss 21-23), dealing in chips the owner put on the market (s 24), or acting for the Commonwealth's defence or security (s 25); whether an action lies (not for acts before Part II commenced, s 7); whether damages, rather than only an account of profits, may be awarded (s 27(3)); and the last day I can be sued (6 years, s 28). DRAFT, not reviewed by an Australian lawyer.
GIVEN c IS A `Layout case`  @desc The layout's making, originality, maker and first exploitation; my act, its day and purpose; any licence, knowledge or acquisition facts
GIVETH A `Layout position`
`the layout position for` c MEANS
    `Layout position` OF `the layout is eligible` c, `the end of the protection period for` c, `my act infringes` c, `an action lies` c, `damages may be awarded` c, `the last day to sue for` c
